== Chain driven (the exact backend path behind kbengine.clone.export)
materialize: loadDemoGameTemplateEntries(templates/assets) -> real project tree in tmpdir
  (same entries the kbengine.project.createDemoGame command writes; Avatar.def landed)
def->tables: getDatabaseSchemaSnapshot('Avatar', <project>) -> 13 tables (tbl_Avatar + 12 child,
  incl two-level tbl_Avatar_bag -> tbl_Avatar_bag_items)
probe:       probePhysicalTables vs information_schema on the real kode_demo DB (MariaDB 11.8.6 local)
plan:        planCloneExport -> Rust RPC $/kode/dbClone/planExport vs packaged bin/kode-server
export:      executeExportPlan (SET TRANSACTION READ ONLY + consistent snapshot, streaming, root-id
  filter WHERE id = ? / parent-id per child) -> 4 typed rows for dbid=1
archive:     writeCloneArchive -> avatar-export.kdpclone (Rust) -> inspectCloneArchive
  (entity=Avatar rows=4) -> readCloneArchiveRows (4 rows back, byte-faithful)

